  "id": "COMPOUND:22706 - PROTEIN:1915",
  "verbalization": "Lupinifolin is shown to interact with T47D cells, a human breast cancer cell line, and this interaction is mediated through a complex molecular pathway. The target of Lupinifolin is T47D, which is also a target of multiple compounds, including a metabolite and a structural isomer of L-Leucine. These compounds all ultimately direct their activity to Aconitate hydratase, a mitochondrial enzyme involved in the biosynthesis of acetyl-CoA. The evidence suggests that Lupinifolin may inhibit Aconitate hydratase, potentially disrupting mitochondrial metabolism. The presence of multiple targets and their shared pathway to Aconitate hydratase supports a mechanistic link between Lupinifolin and the enzyme, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Aconitate hydratase in cellular metabolism and suggests that Lupinifolin may act as a competitive inhibitor of this enzyme.",
